@startuml
actor Client
participant Gateway
participant "Auth Service" as Auth
participant "Account Service" as Account
participant Keycloak

== User Registration ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /auth/register\n(username, email, password, ...)
Gateway -> Auth: Forward /auth/register
Auth -> Keycloak: Create user via Admin REST API
Keycloak --> Auth: User created\n(Keycloak User ID)
Auth -> Account: Create profile with Keycloak User ID
Account --> Auth: Profile created
Auth --> Gateway: 201 Created (user registered)
Gateway --> Client: Success response

== Forgot Password ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /auth/forgot-password\n(email)
Gateway -> Auth: Forward /auth/forgot-password
Auth -> Keycloak: Trigger reset email (Admin REST API)
Keycloak --> Auth: 200 OK
Auth --> Gateway: Success message
Gateway --> Client: Password reset email sent

== Login Flow ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /auth/login\n(username, password)
Gateway -> Auth: Forward /auth/login
Auth -> Keycloak: POST /realms/{realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Keycloak --> Auth: JWT (access + refresh tokens)
Auth --> Gateway: JWT
Gateway --> Client: JWT

== Access Protected Resource ==
Client -> Gateway: GET /accounts/me\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
Gateway -> Account: Forward request with JWT
Account -> Keycloak: Validate JWT (public key / introspection)
Keycloak --> Account: Valid
Account --> Gateway: Account details (JSON)
Gateway --> Client: Account details (JSON)

== Refresh Token ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /auth/refresh\n(refresh_token)
Gateway -> Auth: Forward /auth/refresh
Auth -> Keycloak: POST /token (grant_type=refresh_token)
Keycloak --> Auth: New JWT
Auth --> Gateway: New JWT
Gateway --> Client: New JWT
@enduml
